{"id":"palmer-worm","name":"Palmer-Worm","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:palmer-worm"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Palmer-worm","text":"(Heb. gazam). The English word may denote either a caterpillar (as rendered by the LXX.), which wanders like a palmer or pilgrim, or which travels like pilgrims in bands (Joel 1:4; 2:25), the wingless locusts, or the migratory locust in its larva state."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H1501","lemma":"גָּזָם","xlit":"gâzâm","gloss":"a kind of locust","kjv":"palmer-worm","count":3,"share":1},{"strong":"H398","lemma":"אָכַל","xlit":"ʼâkal","gloss":"to eat","kjv":"at all, burn up, consume, devour","count":3,"share":1}],"verses":["Joel.1.4","Joel.2.25","Amos.4.9"],"related":[{"id":"diet-of-the-jews","type":"lexical","strong":"H398","why":"both lead with אָכַל (H398)"},{"id":"eating","type":"lexical","strong":"H398","why":"both lead with אָכַל (H398)"},{"id":"elijah","type":"lexical","strong":"H398","why":"both lead with אָכַל (H398)"},{"id":"entertainments","type":"lexical","strong":"H398","why":"both lead with אָכַל (H398)"},{"id":"gluttony","type":"lexical","strong":"H398","why":"both lead with אָכַל (H398)"},{"id":"hospitality","type":"lexical","strong":"H398","why":"both lead with אָכַל (H398)"}],"works":[]}
